power solutions, platform engineering, sustainment, and supply chain management for the U.S. government and allied nations. The company was incorporated in 2023 and is headquartered in Chantilly, Virginia.","ceo_bio":"Mr. John E. Heller | CEO & Director | Age 63 | Compensation: $3.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 50K people. Revenue per employee of $288K ranks in the below the sector median among Industrials peers. Each employee generates $10K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $420 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 11\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Amentum Holdings, Inc. is a mid-cap industrials business with a $5.0B market cap on $14.4B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +72% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 3% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $516M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 4 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 8.23\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 6.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 1.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.3\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":